ource category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit> <nplcit status="new"><text>MALM J., BJORK P., GRONOWITZ S., HORNFELDT A.B.: 'Palladium-catalyzed coupling of heteroaryl alkylstannanes with heteroaryl halides in the presence of silver(I)oxide' TETRAHEDRON LETT., vol. 33, no. 16, 1992, pages 2199 - 2202, XP002931101</text> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1186597A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SANKIO CHEMICAL CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUDA HIROKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UMIHARA KEN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SANKIO CHEMICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUDA, HIROKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UMIHARA, KEN</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUDA HIROKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UMIHARA KEN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUDA, HIROKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UMIHARA, KEN</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for the production of 2-pyridylpyridine derivatives usable as intermediates of drugs or agricultural chemicals, which neither requires any expensive special catalyst or special equipment nor causes environmental pollution and can be carried out even on an industrial scale. This process comprises reacting an acetyl-substituted pyridine derivative with a 3-aminoacrolein compound and reacting the obtained product with ammonia or an ammonium salt.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de production de dérivés de 2-pyridylpyridine pouvant être utilisés comme intermédiaires de médicaments ou comme produits chimiques agricoles. Ce procédé n'exige pas de catalyseur coûteux ni d'équipement spécial; il ne cause pas de pollution environnementale et peut même être utilisé à l'échelle industrielle. Ledit procédé consiste à faire réagir un dérivé de pyridine substitué par acétyl avec un composé de 3-amino-acroléine et à faire réagir le produit ainsi obtenu avec de l'ammoniac ou un sel d'ammoniac.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>